<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT-Ahmsa estimates raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Ahmsa estimates raised.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Salomon Brothers raised its 1997 earnings per share estimate for steel maker Altos Hornos de Mexico (Ahmsa) to $0.59 from $0.43, and projected earnings of $0.63 per share for 1998.</p>
<p>-- The brokerage also estimated the company's 1997 operating margin profit will be 19 percent, compared to an estimated 16 percent in 1996 and 20 percent in 1995.</p>
<p>-- &quot;In our view, one of Ahmsa's most attractive points is that significant efficiency gains are still achievable at a relatively low additional cost,&quot; the brokerage said in a report.</p>
<p>-- Salomon has a buy recommendation on the company.</p>
<p>((-- Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
</text>
